{
  "description": "When fdrop's clients retry a request (see 'Java client library' and '.NET client library' in SPEC.md). Both clients' unit tests run every case: 'retry' means a second try is made and its success returned; 'error' a client exception without another try; 'api' the response is returned to the caller after one try.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "failure": "connect-failed",
      "safeToRepeat": true,
      "expect": "retry",
      "why": "the request never reached the server"
    },
    {
      "failure": "connect-failed",
      "safeToRepeat": false,
      "expect": "retry",
      "why": "the request never reached the server"
    },
